# Expected compiler output is compared byte for byte, so git must not rewrite
# it on the way in or out. `core.autocrlf` is on for this repository, and
# without this rule a fresh checkout on Windows would hand the harness CRLF
# while the compiler writes LF, and every case would fail for a reason that has
# nothing to do with the compiler.
#
# `text eol=lf` rather than `-text`: marking them binary would also stop `git
# diff` rendering them, and a regenerated expectation being a readable diff is
# the whole reason regenerating them is safe.
crates/safec/tests/cases/** text eol=lf
